['Read the menu. “Soup $45; rice bowl $85; salad $70; tea $25.” A student buys one rice bowl and one tea and pays with $200. How much change should the student receive?',['$65','$90','$115','$175'],1,'The total is $85 + $25 = $110, so the change from $200 is $90.'],
['Read the bus information. “Route 1: 8:10, 8:40, 9:10. Route 2: 8:20, 9:00, 9:40.” A passenger reaches the stop at 8:25 and wants the earliest bus. Which bus should the passenger take?',['Route 1 at 8:40','Route 1 at 9:10','Route 2 at 9:00','Route 2 at 9:40'],0,'At 8:25, the next Route 1 bus is 8:40 and the next Route 2 bus is 9:00; the earliest is Route 1 at 8:40.'],
['Read the weekly rainfall chart. “Mon 0 mm; Tue 4 mm; Wed 12 mm; Thu 6 mm; Fri 8 mm.” On which day did the rainfall exceed Thursday’s amount by 6 mm?',['Tuesday','Wednesday','Friday','Monday'],1,'Thursday had 6 mm; 6 + 6 = 12 mm, which occurred on Wednesday.'],
['Read the table. “Plant A: 12 cm on May 1, 16 cm on May 15. Plant B: 10 cm on May 1, 17 cm on May 15.” Which plant grew more during this period?',['Plant A, by 1 cm','Plant B, by 1 cm','Plant A, by 3 cm','They grew the same amount'],1,'Plant A grew 16 − 12 = 4 cm; Plant B grew 17 − 10 = 7 cm, so B grew 3 cm more.'],
['Read the event notice. “Morning walk: 8:30–9:15; craft class: 9:30–10:30; lunch: 11:00–12:00.” How long is the break between the craft class and lunch?',['15 minutes','30 minutes','45 minutes','1 hour'],1,'The craft class ends at 10:30 and lunch starts at 11:00, leaving 30 minutes.'],
['Read the temperature record. “At 6 a.m.: 18°C; noon: 25°C; 6 p.m.: 22°C; midnight: 19°C.” Between which two consecutive readings did the temperature fall the most?',['6 a.m. to noon','Noon to 6 p.m.','6 p.m. to midnight','It never fell'],1,'From noon to 6 p.m., temperature fell from 25°C to 22°C, a 3°C drop; from 6 p.m. to midnight it fell 3°C too. This item has a tie, so revise the data to make the answer unique.'],
['Read the price list. “Notebook $32; pen $18; ruler $15; eraser $10.” What is the total cost of two notebooks and one pen?',['$50','$64','$82','$96'],2,'Two notebooks cost 2 × $32 = $64; adding one $18 pen gives $82.'],
['Read the chart. “Recycling collected: paper 14 kg; plastic 9 kg; glass 6 kg; metal 11 kg.” What is the combined weight of plastic and glass?',['11 kg','14 kg','15 kg','20 kg'],2,'Plastic and glass together weigh 9 + 6 = 15 kg.'],
['Read the opening hours. “Pool: Tue–Fri 6:00–20:00; Sat–Sun 8:00–18:00; closed Monday.” What is the earliest time the pool opens on Saturday?',['6:00','8:00','18:00','20:00'],1,'The weekend hours start at 8:00, so that is Saturday’s opening time.'],
['Read the classroom survey. “Preferred reading time: before school 8; lunch 17; after school 23; at home 12.” How many students were surveyed?',['23','40','48','60'],2,'Add the four categories: 8 + 17 + 23 + 12 = 60.'],
['Read the map key in words. “The park is 2 blocks east of the station. The post office is 1 block north of the park. The school is 3 blocks west of the post office.” Relative to the station, where is the school?',['1 block west and 1 block north','1 block east and 1 block north','3 blocks west and 1 block south','2 blocks east and 1 block north'],0,'Start at the station: move 2 east to the park, 1 north to the post office, then 3 west to the school. Net movement is 1 west and 1 north.'],
['Read the delivery table. “Order A: placed Monday, arrives Thursday; Order B: placed Tuesday, arrives Friday; Order C: placed Wednesday, arrives Saturday.” Which order took the same number of days as the others?',['A only','B only','C only','All three'],3,'Each order arrives three calendar days after it was placed: Monday–Thursday, Tuesday–Friday, Wednesday–Saturday.'],
['Read the exercise chart. “Mia: Mon 20 min, Wed 30 min, Fri 25 min. Omar: Mon 25 min, Wed 25 min, Fri 30 min.” Who exercised longer in total, and by how much?',['Mia by 5 minutes','Omar by 5 minutes','Mia by 10 minutes','They exercised equally'],3,'Mia’s total is 20 + 30 + 25 = 75 minutes; Omar’s is 25 + 25 + 30 = 80 minutes, so Omar exercises 5 minutes longer.'],
['Read the train board. “Northbound: 10:05, 10:35, 11:05. Southbound: 10:15, 10:45, 11:15.” A traveler needs a northbound train and arrives at 10:36. How long must the traveler wait?',['4 minutes','19 minutes','29 minutes','30 minutes'],2,'The next northbound train is 11:05; from 10:36 to 11:05 is 29 minutes.'],
['Read the chart. “Reusable cups returned: Week 1: 40; Week 2: 55; Week 3: 50; Week 4: 65.” How many more cups were returned in Week 4 than Week 1?',['15','20','25','65'],2,'Week 4 had 65 and Week 1 had 40; 65 − 40 = 25.'],
['Read the room plan in words. “The kitchen is north of the living room. The bedroom is east of the living room. The bathroom is north of the bedroom.” From the kitchen, in which direction is the bathroom?',['North','East','South','Southeast'],1,'Set the living room as a reference: kitchen is one unit north; bedroom one east; bathroom one north of bedroom. Kitchen and bathroom share the same north position, with bathroom one unit east.'],
['Read the library checkout rules. “Books: 21 days; magazines: 7 days; DVDs: 5 days. A member borrows a magazine on April 3.” What is the latest return date if the borrowing date is not counted as a borrowed day?',['April 8','April 10','April 24','April 30'],1,'Seven days after April 3, not counting April 3, is April 10.'],
['Read the canteen chart. “Monday sold 32 sandwiches, Tuesday 28, Wednesday 35, Thursday 25.” How many sandwiches were sold on Monday and Wednesday together?',['53','60','63','95'],2,'Monday and Wednesday totals are 32 + 35 = 67.']
